# Rabbit Backend Update — Order/Client Authorization Hardening Completed

## Status

Order/client authorization hardening is now implemented and tested successfully.

The order module is now role-aware for V1.

---

## Purpose

The goal was to prevent order data leaks and prevent clients/suppliers from performing unauthorized order actions.

Before hardening, the order module had these risks:

```text
GET /orders could expose all orders.
GET /orders/{orderId} could expose another client's order.
POST /orders trusted client_id from the request body.
PATCH /orders/{orderId}/status needed strict owner-only protection.
Suppliers could potentially reach order endpoints if not blocked.

After hardening:

Owner can manage all orders.
Client can only create and view their own orders.
Supplier cannot access orders.
Only owner can update order status.
Final Authorization Rules
Owner
GET /orders
→ sees all orders

GET /orders/{orderId}
→ can view any order

POST /orders
→ can create an order for a chosen client by sending client_id

PATCH /orders/{orderId}/status
→ can update order status
Client
GET /orders
→ sees only their own orders

GET /orders/{orderId}
→ can view only their own order

POST /orders
→ creates order for themselves

PATCH /orders/{orderId}/status
→ forbidden

Important rule:

When the logged-in user is a client, the backend ignores client_id from the request body and uses Auth::id().
Fournisseur / Supplier
GET /orders
→ forbidden

GET /orders/{orderId}
→ forbidden

POST /orders
→ forbidden

PATCH /orders/{orderId}/status
→ forbidden

Suppliers have no order access in V1 unless explicitly allowed later.

