use App\Core\Auth;

Purpose:

Use the logged-in session user and role to authorize order actions.
all()

OrderService::all() was hardened.

Final behavior:

owner → returns all orders
client → returns only orders where order.client_id = Auth::id()
supplier/other → throws authorization error

Implementation shape:

public function all(): array
{
    $role = Auth::role();

    if ($role === 'owner') {
        $orders = $this->orders->findAll();
    } elseif ($role === 'client') {
        $clientId = Auth::id();

        $orders = array_filter(
            $this->orders->findAll(),
            fn ($order) => (int) $order['client_id'] === $clientId
        );

        $orders = array_values($orders);
    } else {
        throw new ValidationException([
            'auth' => ['You are not allowed to view orders.'],
        ]);
    }

    foreach ($orders as &$order) {
        $order['items'] = $this->orders->findItemsByOrderId($order['id']);
    }

    unset($order);

    return ApiResponse::success('Orders fetched successfully', $orders);
}

Note:

This V1 implementation filters after findAll().
It is acceptable for the school project.
Later optimization can add OrderRepository::findByClientId(int $clientId).
