Private Helper Methods Added
resolveClientIdForOrderCreation()
private function resolveClientIdForOrderCreation(array $data): int
{
    $role = Auth::role();

    if ($role === 'client') {
        return Auth::id();
    }

    if ($role === 'owner') {
        if (empty($data['client_id'])) {
            throw new ValidationException([
                'client_id' => ['client_id is required when owner creates an order.'],
            ]);
        }

        return (int) $data['client_id'];
    }

    throw new ValidationException([
        'auth' => ['You are not allowed to create orders.'],
    ]);
}

Purpose:

Centralizes the rule for who the order belongs to.
Prevents clients from impersonating another client by sending another client_id.
authorizeOrderAccess()
private function authorizeOrderAccess(array $order): void
{
    $role = Auth::role();

    if ($role === 'owner') {
        return;
    }

    if ($role === 'client' && (int) $order['client_id'] === Auth::id()) {
        return;
    }

    throw new ValidationException([
        'auth' => ['You are not allowed to access this order.'],
    ]);
}

Purpose:

Protects GET /orders/{orderId}.
authorizeOwnerOnly()
private function authorizeOwnerOnly(): void
{
    if (Auth::role() === 'owner') {
        return;
    }

    throw new ValidationException([
        'auth' => ['Only owner can update order status.'],
    ]);
}

Purpose:

Defense-in-depth protection for PATCH /orders/{orderId}/status.
