StoreOrderRequest Changes
Problem

Before hardening, StoreOrderRequest always required:

client_id

This was wrong for client-created orders because:

client identity should come from session, not request body.
New Validation Behavior

client_id is now optional at request validation level.

Required fields:

items
shipping_address

Optional field:

client_id

If client_id is provided, it must be an integer.

Final validation shape:

public function validate(): void
{
    Validator::make($this->data)
        ->required('items')
        ->required('shipping_address')
        ->validate();

    if (isset($this->data['client_id']) && $this->data['client_id'] !== null && $this->data['client_id'] !== '') {
        Validator::make($this->data)
            ->integer('client_id')
            ->validate();
    }

    if (!is_array($this->data['items']) || count($this->data['items']) === 0) {
        throw new ValidationException([
            'items' => ['Order must contain at least one item.'],
        ]);
    }

    foreach ($this->data['items'] as $index => $item) {
        $this->validateItem($item, $index);
    }
}
clientId()

Changed from returning always int to nullable ?int.

Final shape:

public function clientId(): ?int
{
    if (!isset($this->data['client_id']) || $this->data['client_id'] === null || $this->data['client_id'] === '') {
        return null;
    }

    return (int) $this->data['client_id'];
}
